15 0 obj
<</A 42 0 R /Alt(Images of rice plants affected by various diseases and conditions. \(a\) Bacterial Leaf Blight \(BLB\) shows discolored leaves. \(b\) Bacterial Leaf Streak \(BLS\) displays streaks. \(c\) Bacterial Panicle Blight \(BPB\) has damaged panicles. \(d\) Blast exhibits lesions. \(e\) Brown Spot presents dark spots. \(f\) Dead Heart shows withered plants. \(g\) Downy Mildew features pale leaves. \(h\) Hispa indicates leaf damage. \(i\) Normal plant appears healthy. \(j\) Tungro displays yellowing and stunting.)/K 0/P 8 0 R /Pg 30 0 R /S/Figure/T()>>
endobj
16 0 obj
<</A 43 0 R /Alt(Diagram showing a neural network block with a residual connection. It starts with a 24x24x3 feature map undergoing Expansion Convolution with a factor of three, resulting in a 24x24x9 feature map. This is followed by Depthwise Convolution, maintaining the same dimensions, and then Projection Convolution, returning to a 24x24x3 feature map. The block includes a dashed line indicating the residual connection from the input to the output.)/K 0/P 8 0 R /Pg 31 0 R /S/Figure/T()>>
endobj
17 0 obj
<</A 44 0 R /Alt(Panel A depicts a neural network training phase with data augmentation and attention mechanism embedding, highlighting layers like inverted residual blocks, convolution, and pooling layers. Panel B shows a graph comparing ReLU6 and Swish activation functions, detailing ReLU6 saturation and Swish's smoothness. Panel C illustrates a feature map processing flow involving squeezing, excitation, and scaling, resulting in a recalibrated feature map.)/K 0/P 8 0 R /Pg 32 0 R /S/Figure/T()>>
endobj
18 0 obj
<</A 45 0 R /Alt(Confusion matrix for a classification model with four classes: BLB, blast, brown spot, and tungro. True labels versus predicted labels are compared. The highest accuracies are: BLB with 1439, brown spot with 1155, and tungro with 1353 correct predictions. The heatmap color gradient corresponds to the number of occurrences, from light blue for low values to dark blue for high values.)/K 0/P 8 0 R /Pg 36 0 R /S/Figure/T()>>
endobj
19 0 obj
<</A 46 0 R /Alt(Line graph showing training and validation loss over 45 epochs for two models: Li-MobileNetV2 and LiS-MobileNetV2. Li-MobileNetV2 Training Loss \(blue\) and Validation Loss \(orange\) decrease steadily, with Validation Loss peaking early. LiS-MobileNetV2 Training Loss \(green\) closely follows the same trend with lower starting loss. Validation Loss \(red\) also shows early peaks. Both models stabilize around epoch 20.)/K 0/P 8 0 R /Pg 37 0 R /S/Figure/T()>>
endobj
20 0 obj
<</A 47 0 R /Alt(Multiple confusion matrices compare the performance of four MobileNetV2 models \(A, B, C, D\) on multi-class classification tasks with labels including BLB, BLS, BPB, blast, brown spot, dead heart, downy mildew, hispa, normal, and tungro. Each matrix shows the true label versus the predicted label with varying intensities of blue indicating the frequency of correct and incorrect classifications.)/K 0/P 8 0 R /Pg 38 0 R /S/Figure/T()>>
endobj
21 0 obj
<</A 48 0 R /Alt(Original images of rice plants affected by four conditions: BLB, BLS, blast, and hispa are shown on the left. To the right are heatmaps generated using MobileNetV2, Li-MobileNetV2, LiA-MobileNetV2, and LiSA-MobileNetV2, highlighting areas of interest in varying shades of green, yellow, and red.)/K 0/P 8 0 R /Pg 39 0 R /S/Figure/T()>>
endobj
